All good ideas but why not just make some of the rarer ones that little bit (
or even a lot) tougher? I like the way dragons have more hits in 3.1, I'm 
less keen on the toning down of the ochre jelly acid splash. My 20+ level 
characters *always* had a healthy respect for those suckers in 3.0. I like 
your idea of having some monsters that are unaffected by some forms of 
attack. Its too easy to carve your way from the castle to ascension without 
your +6 ExcalBringer Blade ever leaving your hand!

Also, maybe reflection should be made an imperfect property, there should be 
a chance that the ray gets through. This would mean that your character 
would have to be more careful faced with ray attack creatures.

Also I find it a little hard to believe that dragon breath can be reflected 
wholly by that silver dinnerplate attached to my arm. Some of it should get 
through!

